      "id": "amentum-space-gravity",
      "name": "Gravity API",
      "description": "The gravitational field of the earth is non-uniform.  The <a href='https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geoid'>geoid</a> is the shape the  ocean surface would take if only gravity and the rotation of the Earth   were considered. The geoid is the surface that defines zero elevation.<br><br>  The geoid height is the difference between an ideal reference ellipsoid  and the geoid.<br><br> The gravity anomaly is the difference between the acceleration due to gravity on the Earth's surface and the value c...",
